The learnr2 package as a whole is released under the MIT license
(see the LICENSE file; copyright holder: learnr2 authors).

It bundles the 'quarto-live' Quarto extension, unmodified, under
inst/extdata/_extensions/r-wasm/live/ (copied into a tutorial's directory by
add_live_extension() and create_tutorial()). That directory keeps its own
LICENSE.md. Its components, and the libraries compiled into its two minified
JavaScript bundles, are under the following licenses -- all permissive and
compatible with MIT:

  Component                                   License
  ------------------------------------------  -------------
  quarto-live (the extension itself)          MIT
  tinyyaml.lua                                MIT
  CodeMirror 6 and Lezer                      MIT
  codemirror-lang-r and lezer-r               MIT
  Comlink                                     Apache-2.0
  @jupyter-widgets/html-manager               BSD-3-Clause
  Pyodide (JavaScript loader only)            MPL-2.0

Copyright holders, upstream URLs, and the location of the unminified sources
for each component are listed in inst/COPYRIGHTS, and the copyright holders
appear with 'cph' roles in the Authors@R field of DESCRIPTION.
